      "writtenOn": "2023-12-21T17:13:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes. this was the whole purpose of this. `tpm` channel is for high level things, see commit message, and `tpmreg` includes all register and state changes. Both can be enabled at the same time if needed \u003d same behavior as before.\n\n`%ph` is very fast and rather compact. I think that it is possible to remove many other fields as command code is in these 10 bytes.",
